     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This is a resubmission of my original post, with a minimal working example (MWE) at the suggestion of a member.</div><div><br></div><div>MWE taken from <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density2d.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density2d.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792370338355000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2IfHtoHjXYcn_u9pwvRuCo\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density2d.html</a></div><div><br></div><div>Given the plot created by the following code:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MASS&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geyser</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MASS&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>m </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geyser</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> duration</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> waiting</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xlim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ylim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">40</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">110</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>m </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_density2d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density2d-4.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density2d-4.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792370338355000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0D5yFUk6_om1uoZERAGRBA\"><img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/tzT0lhNCH1-4_xoudprNcRxOE7J9N0N-BwkZSmYRaq9P7GdN6ScsHXWHAJBZeOG6JDCQIscWM7T9EGD43UP4zUuQ-UYF2f0=s0-d-e1-ft#http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density2d-4.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">I would like to extract the coordinates and density estimates for local and global maxima. For example, the coordinates for maxima in this plot would be something like (1.95,82), (4.05,78), (4.40,54). </p></div>"
